# Gonti, Night Minister: "Whenever a creature deals combat damage to one of your opponents, its controller looks at the top
# card of that opponent's library and exiles it face down. They may play that card ..." (CR 608.2c, 109.5). In a game of
# three Bot1 controls Gonti and Bot2's Memnite hits Bot3 on turn 5: Bot3 is Bot1's opponent, so Bot1's Gonti triggers, and
# the card goes to the creature's controller, Bot2, not to Gonti's: the Ornithopter off the top of Bot3's library (Bot3's
# library 12 -> 11) is cast by Bot2 from exile. It is a spell Bot2 does not own, so Bot2 - the player who cast it, not
# Gonti's controller - creates a Treasure token.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Gonti, Night Minister
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Memnite
Island x19

[Bot3 Deck]
Island x8
Ornithopter
Island x11

